519 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 224 0 R /Rect [ 56.696999 462.644961 538.617004 746.084964 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure2) /TU (A diagram illustrating a process for EEG data analysis. It involves three main stages: raw EEG input and Level-1 segmentation, multi-scale Level-2 segmentation using sliding windows, and rPSD feature extraction with tensor generation. The raw EEG data is divided into coarse segments and further into sub-segments. Each sub-segment undergoes FFT and rPSD for seven bands, producing a multi-scale feature tensor. Multiple colored arrows indicate data flow through each step.) /Type /Annot >>
